module main

# B1 gate regression (finding ②): an UNDER-APPLIED vector_get_direct on a
# `Vector Double` must still reach translate_partial_application and build a
# closure — the B1 gate only intercepts the fully-applied call. Pre-fix the gate
# fired on arg0 alone and hard-Err'd here ("expects 2 arguments"). This fixture
# must COMPILE, and must NOT emit the inlined read.
#
# The missing argument is written `_` because Sprout is n-ary: a bare
# `vector_get_direct(v)` is not partial application but an arity error, rejected with
# "expects 2 arguments, got 1 (Sprout is n-ary; use `_` for partial application)".
# This fixture predates that syntax and sat RED on master for as long as it took
# someone to run `just b1-gate` by hand — which is the same rot the c-runtime-test
# and gate-audit work in this change addresses.
fn get_at(v: Vector Double) -> (Int -> Double !{IO}) =
  vector_get_direct(v, _)
